  'c8', 'GATE', 'SINGLE', 'clinical',
  NULL, NULL, 'What is the age criteria and major exclusion factor for heart valve donation?',
  NULL, 'South African criteria state the range plainly: deceased individuals from the age of 6 months up to and including 55 years can donate heart valves. Valves cannot be donated where death was caused by septicaemia, cancer, poisoning, blood-borne infection or trauma to the heart, or where the cause of death is unknown. Note that this range is valve-specific and much narrower than the 16-to-80-year range that applies to skin, bone, ligaments and tendons — the tissue types carry different criteria and must not be quoted interchangeably.', 'gate-clinical',
