  NULL, NULL, 'Renal transplantation is the primary treatment of choice for which stage of kidney disease?',
  NULL, 'Renal transplantation is the treatment of choice for end-stage renal disease (CKD stage 5). The KDIGO guideline in fact reaches earlier than the label suggests: candidates with CKD G4–G5 (GFR below 30 mL/min/1.73 m²) expected to progress should already be informed about and considered for transplantation, referral should come 6–12 months before anticipated dialysis, and pre-emptive transplantation is recommended once eGFR falls below 10 mL/min/1.73 m², or earlier with symptoms. Transplantation before dialysis is preferred, not a later rescue.', 'gate-clinical',
